<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australia sets wheat shipment record in Jan.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australia sets wheat shipment record in Jan.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's balance of payments, already boosted by big wheat shipments in December, was due for another fillip with a record wheat shipment by the Australian Wheat Board (AWB) in January, the AWB said in a statement.</p>
<p>The 2.1 million tonnes shipped in January was a 300,000 tonne increase on the previous record, set by the AWB in December, it said.</p>
<p>The extra 300,000 tonnes of wheat was worth about US$45.0 million, or A$60.0 million, it said.  </p>
<p>During the next three months the AWB hoped to achieve the same or better results by stretching transport resources to the limit, Malcolm McMahon, AWB general manager Australia division, said.</p>
<p>The shipment represented significant savings for producers, with the cost of storing wheat A$2.00 a tonne a month, he said.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
